#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# SERVE THE CHESS PAGE -- a board in the visitor's own runtime, the hall and
# two ranked tables in this one -- over TLS.
#
#     etcs modules/ChessProvider/scripts/serve_chess.etcs
#     then open https://localhost:8444/
#
# Same shape as serve_paint.etcs: the two isolation headers a -pthread build's
# Workers die without (`wasmMemory is undefined`), the runtime mounted from
# bin/wasm rather than copied beside the page, and every mount spelled from
# ACE_ROOT so the cwd does not matter. Port 8444, not 8443, so this and the
# paint page can run side by side.
#
# Generate a self-signed cert first, once (see NetworkProvider/scripts/
# tls_server.etcs for why the -addext line is not optional):
#
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -days 30 \
#     -keyout /tmp/etcs-key.pem -out /tmp/etcs-cert.pem \
#     -subj "/CN=localhost" \
#     -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:localhost,IP:127.0.0.1"

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8444)
web.EnableTLS(/tmp/etcs-cert.pem /tmp/etcs-key.pem)

# Cross-origin isolation, which is what makes SharedArrayBuffer -- and
# therefore threads, and therefore ChessOpEvent's blocking wait -- available
# at all. Confirm from the page's console with `crossOriginIsolated,
# typeof SharedArrayBuffer`: true / "function".
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin)
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
# The hub every link goes through: /link/hall, /link/table1, and /link/<id>
# for a game a visitor hosts through here (Room.HostVia).
web.spawn(NetworkProvider::LinkHub links)
tree.LoadFromDisk(ACE_ROOT/modules/ChessProvider/scripts/www)
tree.SetDefaultExtension(.html)

# The shared artifact directory, at the path every page in this tree resolves
# against first (WASM_BASE_CANDIDATES, index.html).
tree.MountTree(wasm ACE_ROOT/bin/wasm)

# The site's own icons, so the page wears the same mark here as it does served
# from anticurrententropy.com.
tree.MountTree(favicon ACE_ROOT/scripts/www/favicon)

# The scripts the page stages (www/modules.json), each at the path the OS
# side reads it from -- one list, in chess_mounts.etcs, for every server.
run chess_mounts.etcs tree=tree

# The whole served surface: a name the page asks for and this does not list is
# a 404 waiting to happen.
tree.ListPaths()

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()

# THE HALL AND THE TABLES, on the hub above (chess_service.etcs): the name
# server every casual game uses, and the two games this runtime judges.
run chess_service.etcs links=links
